      "body": "- The prefill CUDA graph's captured full top-k (`FullTopKIndexer._deep_gemm_prefill_captured`) now selects each row up to its own length with `topk_transform_paged_from_metadata`, the selection the decode path already runs on the same paged logits, instead of a `torch.topk` over the whole captured width.\n- The v1 kernel takes `k` from the output width and caps it at 1024 (`kMaxTopK` in `deepseek_v4/topk_v1.cuh`, now `TOPK_V1_MAX_K`). Outputs wider than that keep the torch top-k over `min(k, width)` columns, so no configured `k` is truncated.\n- `TestDSV4FullTopKCapturedFallback` checks which path each output width takes, and that the torch path keeps every column.\n\nBehavior change: with `--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable`, DeepSeek-V4.1's ratio-1/2 indexer layers inside the prefill graph select with the per-row kernel (`index_topk` is 512 for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash).\n\nChecked on GB300 with DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, TP4 (DSPARK, chunked prefill 8192, decoder replay on), against main (617c8b67b1) with the same prefill graph:\n\n- `test_deepseek_v4.py` passes on GB300 (27 tests).\n- GSM8K (sgl-eval, 200 questions, the model's preset, 8-shot prefix): 98.0%, against main's 97.5%.\n- First-token top-20 distributions on prompts that replay the graph (590 to 14,795 tokens), as total variation distance from main eager: at most 0.073; main's graph is at 0.133 on the same prompt, and a second main eager run at 0.088.\n- TTFT, one request, median of 3:\n\n| New tokens | main (ms) | this PR (ms) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 256 | 34.6 | 34.7 |\n| 1,024 | 44.9 | 41.8 |\n| 8,000 | 109.8 | 101.1 |\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39192645755](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39192645755)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39192645634](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39192645634)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:en